<surname>Pranpat</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bradner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Inhibition of histone deacetylase 6 acetylates and disrupts the chaperone function of heat shock protein 90: a novel basis for antileukemia activity of histone deacetylase inhibitors</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2005</year><volume>280</volume><fpage>26729</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15937340</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-co15-5-237"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glaser</surname><given-names>KB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><sc>hdac</sc> inhibitors: clinical update and mechanism-based potential</article-title><source>Biochem Pharmacol</source><year>2007</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>659</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17498667</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-co15-5-237"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khochbin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Verdel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lemercier</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Seigneurin&#x02013;Berny</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional significance of histone deacetylase diversity</article-title><source>Curr Opin Genet Dev</source><year>2001</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>162</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11250139</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-co15-5-237"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>XJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Seto</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Rpd3/Hda1 family of lysine deacetylases: from bacteria and yeast to mice and men</article-title><source>Nat Rev Mol Cell Biol</source><year>2008</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>206</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18292778</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-co15-5-237"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grozinger</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Schreiber</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Deacetylase enzymes: biological functions and the use of small-molecule inhibitors</article-title><source>Chem Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11841934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-co15-5-237"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walkinshaw</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tahmasebi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bertos</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>XJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Histone deacetylases as transducers and targets of nuclear signaling</article-title><source>J Cell Biochem</source><year>2008</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>1541</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18425769</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19-co15-5-237"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fischle</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Dequiedt</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Hendzel</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Enzymatic activity associated with class <sc>ii</sc> <sc>hdacs</sc> is dependent on a multiprotein complex containing Hdac3 and Smrt/N-CoR</article-title><source>Mol Cell</source><year>2002</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>45<